---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const research = {
  title: 'Market Trends 2024-2025',
  date: '2026-09-15',
  category: 'Market Analysis',
  excerpt: 'Comprehensive analysis of emerging market trends, consumer behavior shifts, and industry dynamics.'
};
---

<BaseLayout title={research.title} description={research.excerpt}>
  <article class="py-16">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="mb-8">
        <div class="flex gap-4 mb-4 text-sm">
          <span class="text-slate-500">{research.date}</span>
          <span class="text-blue-600 font-semibold">{research.category}</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4 text-slate-900">{research.title}</h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-slate-600">{research.excerpt}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
        <h2>Executive Summary</h2>
        <p>
          The global business environment continues to evolve rapidly, shaped by technological advancement, geopolitical tensions, and changing consumer expectations. Organizations must navigate these shifts strategically to maintain competitive advantage.
        </p>

        <h2>Key Market Trends</h2>
        
        <h3>1. AI and Automation Acceleration</h3>
        <p>
          Artificial intelligence adoption is accelerating across industries, from customer service to drug discovery. Organizations investing in AI capabilities today are positioning themselves for significant competitive advantage.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>GenAI tools becoming mainstream in enterprise workflows</li>
          <li>Skills gap creating talent competition</li>
          <li>Regulatory frameworks emerging across regions</li>
          <li>Integration challenges with legacy systems</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>2. Sustainability as Competitive Necessity</h3>
        <p>
          ESG considerations are no longer optional. Investors, customers, and regulators increasingly factor environmental and social performance into decisions.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Supply chain transparency becoming mandatory</li>
          <li>Carbon pricing mechanisms expanding globally</li>
          <li>Consumer preference for sustainable brands growing</li>
          <li>Regulatory requirements increasing complexity</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>3. Hybrid Work Maturation</h3>
        <p>
          Remote work has become permanent for many organizations. The focus has shifted from enabling remote work to optimizing hybrid models and maintaining culture.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Office redesign for collaboration and connection</li>
          <li>Talent attraction through flexibility</li>
          <li>Time zone coordination challenges</li>
          <li>Measuring productivity and engagement</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>4. Supply Chain Resilience Focus</h3>
        <p>
          Lessons from recent disruptions have led organizations to prioritize supply chain resilience over pure efficiency.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Nearshoring and diversification strategies</li>
          <li>Real-time visibility and monitoring</li>
          <li>Supplier relationship deepening</li>
          <li>Inventory buffers increasing</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Consumer Behavior Shifts</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Personalization Expectations:</strong> Customers expect hyper-personalized experiences across all touchpoints</li>
          <li><strong>Value Consciousness:</strong> Even affluent consumers seek value and are comparing options</li>
          <li><strong>Experience Premium:</strong> Willingness to pay for convenient, seamless experiences</li>
          <li><strong>Purpose Alignment:</strong> Brand values increasingly influence purchase decisions</li>
          <li><strong>Digital-First Expectations:</strong> Seamless online and offline integration required</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Industry-Specific Implications</h2>
        <p>
          Different industries face unique challenges and opportunities. Strategic responses must be tailored to industry dynamics while leveraging these broad trends.
        </p>

        <h2>Strategic Recommendations</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Invest in AI capabilities aligned with customer value creation</li>
          <li>Build supply chain resilience and transparency</li>
          <li>Develop sustainability strategy integrated with business model</li>
          <li>Create hybrid work model supporting productivity and culture</li>
          <li>Enhance customer experience through personalization and omnichannel integration</li>
          <li>Build organizational agility to respond to continued uncertainty</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>